      "qualification": {
        "pointer": "/case/sections/2/blocks/0",
        "quote": "Start with the macroscopic question in Fig. 1b/c: does the liquid still flow when the vial is tilted? In 10 mM PBS at pH 7.4, 5% (w/v) lPGS-15TA forms a self-supporting gel after 5 min at 370 nm and 25 mW/cm². A 10% lPGS-3TA solution remains a solution even after 60 min. The percentages are mass/volume concentrations: 5% w/v means 5 g polymer per 100 mL solution, not the mass fraction of TA in the polymer. These photographs differ simultaneously in TA loading, concentration and irradiation time. They show outcomes for the tested formulations, not the isolated causal effect of TA loading."
      }
    },
