      "qualification": {
        "pointer": "/case/sections/3/blocks/4",
        "quote": "Fig. 2c/d asks a different question: with each formulation fixed, how does irradiation time change elasticity? Each point comes from a separately irradiated vial followed by rheology, not continuous in-situ measurement of one vial. G′ rises markedly after about 3 min for 8% 6TA and from about 2 min for 5% 15TA, then increases more slowly. The authors describe saturation, but this does not establish complete reaction of every TA group. Comparing c with d changes both TA loading and polymer mass concentration; their modulus difference cannot be assigned wholly to one variable."
      }
    },
